'@@author Rixte
@startuml
!include ../shortfall/style.iuml
title Execution: validate the current position, then replace the recipe
autonumber

participant "MishMash" as App
participant "edit: EditRecipeCommand" as Edit
participant "changes: RecipeChanges" as Changes
participant "book: RecipeBook" as Book
participant "original: Recipe" as Original
participant "edited: Recipe" as Edited
participant "viewer: RecipeViewer" as Viewer

note over Edit, Changes : Parsing has produced an edit for index 1 with p/55.
App -> Edit : execute(book)
activate Edit
Edit -> Book : size()
Book --> Edit : recipeCount
alt book is empty or index exceeds recipeCount
  Edit --> App : throws MishMashException
  note over Edit, Book : No replacement occurs; the caller displays the error.
else selected position exists
  Edit -> Book : getRecipes()
  Book --> Edit : current recipe snapshot
  note over Edit, Book : Select original = snapshot.get(index - 1).
  Edit -> Changes : applyTo(original)
  activate Changes
  Changes -> Original : getName()
  Original --> Changes : current name
  note over Changes, Original
    Read the other omitted fields through their getters.
    Use 55 for the supplied protein field.
  end note
  create Edited
  Changes -> Edited : new Recipe(merged fields)
  note right of Edited : Constructor validates the complete replacement recipe.
  Changes --> Edit : edited
  deactivate Changes
  create Viewer
  Edit -> Viewer : new RecipeViewer()
  Edit -> Viewer : view(edited)
  Viewer --> Edit : formatted recipe details
  note over Edit, Viewer : Prepare the complete confirmation before modifying the book.
  Edit -> Book : replace(index - 1, edited)
  Book --> Edit : replacement complete
  Edit --> App : confirmation with updated recipe
end
deactivate Edit

note over Edit, Book
  Repeated size checks, most getters, logging, and formatting details are condensed.
  The book keeps its size and order. The original Recipe object is never mutated.
  Existing plans and groceries retain their original snapshots.
end note
@enduml
'@@author
